# Two binary trees on five taxa.
#
# Both modes return a level-2 network with two reticulations -- van Iersel &
# Kelk (2011) prove the minimum is the same for the tree and softwired-cluster
# models when the input is two binary trees on the same taxon set.
#
# But the minimum is all that coincides. Cluster mode's network happens not to
# display these two trees, only their clusters; display mode's does, for the
# same two reticulations:
#
#   phylocass examples/two_trees.newick                   displays-trees=False
#   phylocass examples/two_trees.newick --display-trees   displays-trees=True
((a,e),(c,(b,d)));
(d,(b,(c,(a,e))));
